---
import Institucional from '../../layouts/Institucional.astro';
import { CORREO_CONTACTO, DOMICILIO } from '../../data/contacto';
import { rutaAvisoLegal } from '../../lib/rutas';

const navegadores = [
  { nombre: 'Google Chrome', href: 'https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647?hl=en' },
  {
    nombre: 'Mozilla Firefox',
    href: 'https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/enhanced-tracking-protection-firefox-desktop',
  },
  { nombre: 'Apple Safari', href: 'https://support.apple.com/en-us/guide/safari/sfri11471/mac' },
  {
    nombre: 'Microsoft Edge',
    href: 'https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09',
  },
];
---

<Institucional
  pagina="privacidad"
  nombre="Privacy policy"
  descripcion="What data is collected when you visit Mejor Eléctrico, what it is used for, which cookies the site and its providers set, and how to exercise your rights."
  actualizado="2026-10-19"
>
  <p>
    At Mejor Eléctrico we collect as little data as possible. You can read the articles and use the comparison tool
    without registering, without giving your name and without filling in forms. This policy explains what information
    is processed when you visit <strong>mejorelectrico.com</strong>, who processes it and how you can control it.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Controller:</strong> Mejor Eléctrico</li>
    <li><strong>Address:</strong> {DOMICILIO}</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Email for privacy matters:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${CORREO_CONTACTO}`}>{CORREO_CONTACTO}</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What data we process</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Browsing data.</strong> When a page loads, your browser automatically sends technical data such as your IP
      address, browser and device type, language and referring page. It is used by the services that host and measure
      the site (see section 4).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Usage statistics.</strong> Google Analytics tells us which pages are visited, for how long, from which
      approximate country and on what type of device. This data is aggregated: we do not use it to identify you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Theme preference.</strong> If you choose the light or dark theme, that choice is saved in your own browser
      (local storage, key <code>tema</code>). It does not leave your device and we do not receive it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Emails you send us.</strong> If you write to us, we process your email address and whatever you tell us,
      only to reply to you.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The site has no comments, user accounts or forms, and we do not ask for sensitive data. Fonts are served from our own
    domain, so loading them does not send data to third parties. The share buttons are plain links: they load nothing
    from WhatsApp, X or Facebook until you click them.
  </p>

  <h2>3. What we use it for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Showing the site and protecting it from attacks and abuse.</li>
    <li>Understanding which content is of most interest and improving the articles and the comparison tool.</li>
    <li>Showing advertising that helps fund the site (see section 6).</li>
    <li>Answering the inquiries, corrections and requests you send us.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The legal basis is your consent for measurement and advertising cookies, and our legitimate interest in keeping the
    site working and secure for the essential technical data. We do not sell your data.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Who it is shared with</h2>
  <p>The data is processed, on our behalf or as independent controllers, by these providers:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which hosts the site and delivers it from servers in different countries. It receives
      the technical data of each visit in order to serve the pages and block malicious traffic.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Supabase</strong>, which stores the spec sheets of the comparison tool. When you open the tool, your browser
      requests the car data from it and, with that request, sends technical data such as your IP address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google</strong>, which provides Google Analytics and, when the site shows ads, Google AdSense. You can read{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites?hl=en" rel="noopener">
        how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a
      >.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these providers process data outside your country, for example in the United States. We work with providers
    that offer adequate protection guarantees. We may also hand over data to an authority when the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">5. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    A cookie is a small file that a site stores in your browser to remember information between one visit and the next.
    Cookies are tied to the browser, not the person, and do not store data such as your name or your card.
  </p>
  <p>Mejor Eléctrico does not set its own cookies. The ones that may appear are from third parties:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Measurement (Google Analytics):</strong> <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>. They distinguish visitors
      and sessions for statistics. They last up to two years. They are only set on mejorelectrico.com.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Advertising (Google AdSense and its partners):</strong> for example <code>__gads</code>,
      <code>__gpi</code> and <code>IDE</code>. They are used to show ads, limit how many times you see the same one and
      measure their performance. They can last up to thirteen months.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you block these cookies, the site works just the same: you can read every article and use the comparison tool.</p>

  <h2>6. Google advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The site may show Google AdSense ads. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your
    prior visits to this or other websites. Advertising cookies enable Google and its partners to show you ads based on
    your browsing on the internet.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can turn off personalized advertising in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener"
      >Google's ad settings</a
    >, and that of other providers at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a> or, if
    you are in Europe, at <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a>. If you turn
    it off, you will still see ads, but they will not be based on your interests.
  </p>
  <p>In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, Google only shows personalized ads with your consent.</p>

  <h2>7. How to control cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can view, block or delete cookies from your browser settings, and reject only third-party ones. Keep in mind that
    the setting is made in each browser and on each device you use:
  </p>
  <ul>
    {
      navegadores.map((navegador) => (
        <li>
          <a href={navegador.href} rel="noopener">
            {navegador.nombre}
          </a>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p>
    To stay out of Google Analytics on every site, you can install <a
      href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout?hl=en"
      rel="noopener">Google's opt-out add-on</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>8. How long it is kept</h2>
  <p>
    Google Analytics statistics are kept for the period set in that tool, which ranges from two to fourteen months.
    Hosting providers' technical logs are kept for the time they set for security. Emails you send us are kept for as long
    as the conversation lasts and a reasonable time to deal with later claims; after that they are deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under Colombia's Law 1581 of 2012 and its regulatory decrees, you have the right to know, update and rectify your
    data; to request proof of the authorization you gave us; to know how we use it; to revoke the authorization or ask us
    to delete it when there is no legal duty to keep it; to consult it free of charge, and to file complaints with the
    Superintendence of Industry and Commerce, the Colombian data protection authority.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you visit the site from the European Union or another country with an equivalent law, such as the General Data
    Protection Regulation (GDPR), you also have the right to request access to, rectification, erasure, restriction and
    portability of your data, to object to its processing and to complain to the data protection authority of your
    country.
  </p>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, write to <a href={`mailto:${CORREO_CONTACTO}`}>{CORREO_CONTACTO}</a>
    with the subject "Personal data" and explain what you need. We answer inquiries within a maximum of ten business days
    and claims within fifteen business days, as set by Colombian law.
  </p>
  <p>
    Since almost all browsing data is processed by Google, Cloudflare and Supabase, the fastest way to control it is often
    your browser settings or those providers' tools. We cannot link that data to your name.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Minors</h2>
  <p>
    The site is aimed at adults and does not knowingly collect data from minors. If you believe a minor has sent us their
    data, write to us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If the way we process data changes, for example when we add a provider, we will update this page and its date. The
    general terms of use of the site are in the <a href={rutaAvisoLegal('en')}>legal notice</a>.
  </p>
</Institucional>
